comments.body:
I was hoping that just changing this `notFoundErrMsg` function to ask the standard library what error message it would use for this situation would be low-risk because it doesn't require refactoring anything outside of test code.

I would agree that making changes to the error handling of the _main_ code should be a separate PR if we intend to do it, because it seems like it means changing some of our internal API designs at least a little.

One thing I noticed looking again at `package syscall` is that they seem to actually define an `ENOENT` constant on Windows, as an alias for `ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND`, presumably for exactly this sort of situation where callers want to ask "what is the errno for `ENOENT`?" without using conditional compilation.

So maybe we could change this to:

```go
func notFoundErrMsg() string {
    return syscall.ENOENT.Error()
}
```

I've not tested this so I can't promise it will work, but if it _does_ work then it seems like a relatively simple workaround for now until we have time to try a deeper change. What do you think?
